{"id":"n-20261027-s45a2q","category":"finance","display_title":"The Economic Cost of Election Day","display_title_he":"העלות הכלכלית של יום הבחירות","short_summary":"An examination of how Israel's national election day shutdown impacts the economy and consumer spending habits.","english_level":"C1","words":432,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/PERSPECTIVE_VIEW_FROM_NORTHWEST_OF_8-14_PARKWAY_%28APARTMENT_BUILDINGS%29._NOTE_PEDESTRIAN_WALKWAY_ON_LEFT._-_Old_Greenbelt%2C_Crescent_Road_and_Southway%2C_Greenbelt%2C_Prince_George%27s_County%2C_HABS_MD-1217-12.tif/lossy-page1-960px-thumbnail.tif.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Rosenthal, James W., creator · Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PERSPECTIVE_VIEW_FROM_NORTHWEST_OF_8-14_PARKWAY_(APARTMENT_BUILDINGS)._NOTE_PEDESTRIAN_WALKWAY_ON_LEFT._-_Old_Greenbelt,_Crescent_Road_and_Southway,_Greenbelt,_Prince_George%27s_County,_HABS_MD-1217-12.tif"},"sources":[{"name":"Walla","domain":"finance.walla.co.il","url":"https://finance.walla.co.il/item/3873598","title":"קלפי, קפה וקניון: כך תימנעו מחגיגת בזבוזים ביום הבחירות","published_at":"2026-10-27T08:51:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-27T08:51:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-27T06:27:04.809Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["In many democratic nations, casting a ballot happens during a regular workday or over the weekend. However, according to data from the Pew Research Center, Israel stands out as one of just sixteen democracies where weekday elections coincide with a national day of rest. This unique arrangement grants citizens a paid mid-week break, closing schools and many workplaces while giving families an opportunity to vote and spend time away from their daily routines.","Yet, this democratic holiday carries substantial financial implications for the entire country. According to an estimate by the Economic Research Department at the Manufacturers Association, the total cost of the election day shutdown to the economy is expected to reach approximately 2.68 billion shekels. Breaking down these figures, about 1.82 billion shekels stems from the business sector, while the public sector accounts for roughly 860 million shekels. While large portions of the economy slow down or halt operations entirely, certain industries experience a notable surge in commercial activity as citizens look for ways to occupy their unexpected free time.","Historical credit card data highlights how consumers utilize this unexpected leisure time. Following the 2022 Knesset elections, transactions processed by Sheba between 7:00 and 22:00 reached approximately 1.346 billion shekels. Similarly, data published from the 2024 local authority elections showed credit card expenditures exceeding 1.5 billion shekels. Detailed spending breakdowns reveal robust activity across various retail sectors, including roughly 211 million shekels spent in supermarket chains, 136.5 million in restaurants, cafes, and fast food, 126 million in clothing and footwear, 106 million in electricity and electronics, and 11.6 million in entertainment and leisure.","This dynamic creates a peculiar economic paradox. On one side of the ledger, the national economy absorbs a massive financial loss because a vast portion of the workforce remains idle. On the other side, that exact same freedom generates an influx of consumer spending as families flock to shopping malls, restaurants, and recreational spots. Citizens typically cast their votes early and then face hours of waiting for news updates and evening exit polls. To break the monotony and escape the constant cycle of news coverage, many people turn to commercial distractions.","Financial experts emphasize that spending money on an election day off is not inherently problematic, provided it aligns with deliberate planning rather than impulsive reactions. Special promotional campaigns launched by retailers can sometimes offer genuine savings on pre-planned purchases, but they can also create artificial desires for items consumers never intended to buy. Developing a basic budget or outlining a general schedule before the polls open can help prevent spending from accumulating passively throughout the day, ensuring that both the ballot and the household wallet are managed with careful consideration."],"facts":[{"fact":"According to the Pew Research Center data, Israel is one of 16 democracies where weekday elections are held on a day designated as a national holiday or day of rest.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"According to estimates from the Economic Research Department at the Manufacturers Association, the cost of the election day shutdown to the economy is expected to reach approximately 2.68 billion shekels.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Out of the total estimated cost, about 1.82 billion shekels comes from the business sector and about 860 million shekels from the public sector.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Following the 2022 Knesset elections, credit card data published by Sheba showed expenses totaling about 1.346 billion shekels between 7:00 and 22:00.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"During the 2024 local authority elections, credit card spending exceeded 1.5 billion shekels.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"democratic","lemma":"democratic","pos":"adjective","he":"דמוקרטי","name":false},{"text":"nations","lemma":"nation","pos":"noun","he":"מדינות","name":false},{"text":"casting","lemma":"cast","pos":"verb","he":"הצבעה","name":false},{"text":"ballot","lemma":"ballot","pos":"noun","he":"פתק הצבעה / קלפי","name":false},{"text":"regular","lemma":"regular","pos":"adjective","he":"רגיל","name":false},{"text":"workday","lemma":"workday","pos":"noun","he":"יום עבודה","name":false},{"text":"weekend","lemma":"weekend","pos":"noun","he":"סוף שבוע","name":false},{"text":"data","lemma":"data","pos":"noun","he":"נתונים","name":false},{"text":"stands out","lemma":"stand out","pos":"verb","he":"בלוט / יוצא דופן","name":false},{"text":"democracies","lemma":"democracy","pos":"noun","he":"דמוקרטיות","name":false},{"text":"weekday","lemma":"weekday","pos":"noun","he":"יום חול","name":false},{"text":"elections","lemma":"election","pos":"noun","he":"בחירות","name":false},{"text":"coincide","lemma":"coincide","pos":"verb","he":"להתרחש בו זמנית","name":false},{"text":"national","lemma":"national","pos":"adjective","he":"לאומי","name":false},{"text":"day of rest","lemma":"day of rest","pos":"noun","he":"יום מנוחה / שבתון","name":false},{"text":"arrangement","lemma":"arrangement","pos":"noun","he":"הסדר","name":false},{"text":"grants","lemma":"grant","pos":"verb","he":"מעניק","name":false},{"text":"citizens","lemma":"citizen","pos":"noun","he":"אזרחים","name":false},{"text":"paid","lemma":"paid","pos":"adjective","he":"ממומן / בתשלום","name":false},{"text":"mid-week","lemma":"mid-week","pos":"adjective","he":"אמצע השבוע","name":false},{"text":"break","lemma":"break","pos":"noun","he":"הפסקה / חופשה","name":false},{"text":"closing","lemma":"close","pos":"verb","he":"סוגר","name":false},{"text":"schools","lemma":"school","pos":"noun","he":"בתי ספר","name":false},{"text":"workplaces","lemma":"workplace","pos":"noun","he":"מקומות עבודה","name":false},{"text":"opportunity","lemma":"opportunity","pos":"noun","he":"הזדמנות","name":false},{"text":"routines","lemma":"routine","pos":"noun","he":"שגרות","name":false},{"text":"holiday","lemma":"holiday","pos":"noun","he":"חג / יום חופש","name":false},{"text":"substantial","lemma":"substantial","pos":"adjective","he":"משמעותי","name":false},{"text":"financial","lemma":"financial","pos":"adjective","he":"פיננסי / כלכלי","name":false},{"text":"implications","lemma":"implication","pos":"noun","he":"השלכות","name":false},{"text":"estimate","lemma":"estimate","pos":"noun","he":"הערכה","name":false},{"text":"shutdown","lemma":"sh